  "answer": "This has been reported before. PowerToys#48516 describes the same behavior after 0.100: when a laptop is docked or undocked or an external monitor is reconnected, the settings page lists only the built-in display, and the dock shows up empty, scales wrongly, or disappears. The cause is that the dock binds to specific monitor devices instead of following Windows' primary/non-primary configuration, as it did in 0.99. PowerToys#49018 reports the empty dock bar on a secondary display, which matches the empty dock you see on the reconnected monitor. The tickets give no confirmed fix or workaround. Add your details (version 0.100.2, ultrawide 3440 plus a 2560 laptop display) to #48516 and watch it for a fix. Until one ships, the only option is to re-enable the dock on the monitor after reconnecting it, though the tickets report that it may still appear empty."
 },
